# macOS and per-developer Xcode state
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate

# Xcode-generated SwiftPM workspace state. Regenerated on open; tracking it
# only produces churn between machines.
/.swiftpm/

# Machine-local scientific corpora and migration snapshots — and, since
# 2026-09-03, the py4DSTEM source lock too: tools/lib/fetch-py4dstem.sh clones
# it at one pinned upstream commit on demand. The inline `DEVIATION` notes in
# Core/ cite that commit's files by line; the pin is the reason they stay true.
/References

# Local build products
/build/
/DerivedData/

# tools/ui-qc-playthrough dev-scoping handoff (see run.sh)
/.ui-qc-filter
/.ui-qc-no-screenshots

# SwiftPM (Package.swift builds DSTEMCore from the shell)
.build/
.swiftpm/

# Model assets never live in the tree (consolidation C2, 2026-09-07). The AGPL
# yolov8n.mlpackage sat in the app target for two days and shipped in nothing;
# trained detector assets are the owner's data under References/.
*.mlpackage
*.mlmodel
*.aimodel
# the one exception (C7, 2026-09-08): the shipping learned disk detector, own weights, pinned by
# its record JSON beside it and hashed into provenance (Models/DiskDetector/README in the record).
# The `/**` is load-bearing: re-including the .mlpackage directory lets git descend into it, but
# every file beneath is still matched on its own, so `*.mlmodel` swallowed the model spec and it
# was never committed. A clone hashed 62b0215f where the record says 0f53d270, the unit gate went
# red on that number, and the app bundled a package with weights and no graph (found 2026-09-09).
!Models/DiskDetector/disk-detector-heatmap-256.mlpackage
!Models/DiskDetector/disk-detector-heatmap-256.mlpackage/**
# the frozen hand-labelled test set is the owner's data (C6); its sha256 and counts are in the evidence file
tools/disk-detector/labels/

# Session evidence: retained logs referenced by docs, never committed
scratchpad/
